WORKING LOG -- AWPTCM-T33357 run 1 -- bench-runner, campaign tb490+tb5 auth 2026-10-29T1304, group A
==========================================================================================
Session facts, devices, client path, clock offset (DUT ~34 s behind the box), host NIC MACs: as recorded in
  auth-2026-10-29T1304/T33375/work/run1.log (same group, same console). In short: tb490 u2 = swi_dut AT-x980-16CDQ
  S/N A10732A263200035 awplus_main-20261029-90; supplicant tb5 eth6 00:90:0b:2a:11:c3; DUT vlan1 192.168.50.1
  e01a.ead5.0456; authenticator port port1.0.81 (EAPOL crosses x530 and x950, both `dot1x eap forward`). No PDU.

CASE: AWPTCM-T33357  (194) Authentication&Security_IEEE 802.1XEncryptionType  - EAP-TLS
  ck.db: status Draft, STEP_BY_STEP, num_steps 1 with an EMPTY step, has_objective 0. Nothing authored beyond the title.
Steps (derived from the title; method as tb277 T9032, 2026-10-23/28):
  S1 provision: local RADIUS user cktls; enroll it against the DUT's own `local` CA (PKCS#12); export the CA (pem
     terminal) and the PKCS#12 (TFTP to tb5); port1.0.81 `dot1x port-control auto`.
  S2 control: a client certificate NOT issued by the DUT's CA (self-signed, CN=cktls) -> EAP-Failure, port Unauthorized, 0/4.
  S3 EAP-TLS with the DUT-issued certificate (supplicant held at TLS 1.2) -> EAP-Success, Mode D Authenticated, 4/4.
  S4 (characterisation) the same with the supplicant's default TLS (1.3 capable) -- memory eap-tls-needs-tls12-supplicant.
Supplicant: tools/wpasup.py (wpa_supplicant on tb5, driver wired; TLS ceiling by per-process OPENSSL_CONF, no root
  change; file work/openssl-tls12.cnf). The tb5 system wpa_supplicant (pid 425, dbus -u -s) was left alone.

